 {"id": "adv#0", "slug": "synthetic", "title": "Writing HTML by hand", "segs": [
  {"id": 1, "kind": "p", "text": "To wrap a block, type <seg id=\"2\"> before it and </seg> after it."},
  {"id": 2, "kind": "p", "text": "Paragraphs start with <p> and end with </p>, and a < b holds when a is smaller."},
  {"id": 3, "kind": "p", "text": "Use `Result<T, E>` for fallible functions and `Option<T>` for optional values."},
  {"id": 4, "kind": "li", "text": "Arrow functions look like `(x) => x * 2` and compare with >= or <=."},
  {"id": 5, "kind": "p", "text": "The closing tag </seg> is not special in this tutorial; it is just text."}
 ]},
